    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78-a6">

                <pb facs="0201" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg107"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tillman to Mr. Dillard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Dillard</hi>: I wrote you several days ago
                    that courtesy demanded that Mr. St. John should make the award of the amount
                    which might be agreed upon between Santos and Ecuador. I have time now to write
                    only a few lines to say that not only does courtesy demand this, but I think it
                    necessary that the amount which he may be willing to accept should be awarded by
                    the arbitrator selected in accordance with the convention. Communicate this to
                    Mr. Santos.</p>
                <p>Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James D. Tillman</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
